Article 17 Inspection of Standards

Inspection of standards for postal service provision facilities must be carried out as follows:

1. The conduct of inspection by the postal authority must have the agreement of the Minister of Technology and Communications;

2. The conduct of inspection by the postal operator must have the agreement of the head of the Technology and Communications Department of the province or capital;

3. Inspection must prepare instruments for the inspection, measurement, and forms for collecting data on inspection results in order to record the inspection, with signature acknowledgment between the inspector and the inspected person;

4. After inspection, if the quality drops below 80%, notification must be sent to the operator for improvement and correction to be completed within sixty days;

5. Inspection must be conducted regularly, starting inspection from November through December of every year.

